{"id":1534,"date":"2026-08-23T19:12:04","date_gmt":"2026-08-23T19:12:04","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/?post_type=knowledgebase&#038;p=1534"},"modified":"2026-08-23T19:37:42","modified_gmt":"2026-08-23T19:37:42","slug":"booklet-printing","status":"publish","type":"knowledgebase","link":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/db\/export-share\/booklet-printing\/","title":{"rendered":"Booklet Printing"},"content":{"rendered":"<div style=\"color: #2b2b2b;\">\n<h2 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Booklet Printing<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1555\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/bookletPrintingWide.webp\" alt=\"Booklet Printing\" width=\"162\" height=\"118\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/bookletPrintingWide.webp 555w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/bookletPrintingWide-300x218.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 162px) 100vw, 162px\" \/><\/span><\/h2>\n<p class=\"western\">Booklet Printing assembles your pages into printer spreads ready for saddle-stitch binding &#8211; ideal for zines, magazines, programmes, and folded brochures. Open Publisher automatically calculates the correct page pairing order so you don&#8217;t have to.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">How to Print a Booklet<br \/>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1546\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/HowToPrintABooklet-wide.webp\" alt=\"How to Print a Booklet\" width=\"165\" height=\"119\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/HowToPrintABooklet-wide.webp 555w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/HowToPrintABooklet-wide-300x216.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 165px) 100vw, 165px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Go to <strong>File &gt; Print Booklet<\/strong>, or select the <strong>Booklet<\/strong> option from the print modal.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Print double-sided on your printer.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Fold and staple through the central spine to complete the booklet.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">How Pages Are Paired<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1537\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-23-201113.png\" alt=\"How Pages Are Paired\" width=\"258\" height=\"265\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-23-201113.png 728w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-23-201113-293x300.png 293w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 258px) 100vw, 258px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">The engine automatically calculates which pages print together on each sheet. For an 8-page document, the pairings are:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Sheet 1 front:<\/strong> Pages 8 + 1<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Sheet 1 back:<\/strong> Pages 2 + 7<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Sheet 2 front:<\/strong> Pages 6 + 3<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Sheet 2 back:<\/strong> Pages 4 + 5<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Background Rendering in Booklet Mode<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1548\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/BookletPrintingInBackground.webp\" alt=\"Background Rendering in Booklet Mode\" width=\"150\" height=\"120\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/BookletPrintingInBackground.webp 555w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/BookletPrintingInBackground-300x240.webp 300w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<p class=\"western\">Page backgrounds applied via <strong>Format Background<\/strong> or the <strong>Theme Studio<\/strong> render correctly in booklet mode. Gradients are physically converted to DOM layers to bypass browser <span style=\"font-family: Courier New, monospace;\">backgroundColor<\/span> limitations, ensuring your backgrounds print faithfully on every spread.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Booklet Printing Booklet Printing assembles your pages into printer spreads ready for saddle-stitch binding &#8211; ideal for zines, magazines, programmes, and folded brochures. Open Publisher automatically calculates the correct page pairing order so you don&#8217;t have to. How to Print a Booklet Go to File &gt; Print Booklet, or select the Booklet option from the [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1560,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","template":"","knowledgebase_cat":[21],"class_list":["post-1534","knowledgebase","type-knowledgebase","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","knowledgebase_cat-export-share"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1534","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/knowledgebase"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1534"}],"version-history":[{"count":17,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1534\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1559,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1534\/revisions\/1559"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1560"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1534"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"knowledgebase_cat","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase_cat?post=1534"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}